4,43298,3,44970,17,13,18,19,11,16,701,16844,626,16119,1188,16,13,21,21,11,15,1106,1502,20912,35,3,44970,16,13,21,21,11,15,701,69214,317,1502,20912,16,19,18,24884,43298,3,44970,16,13,21,21,11,15,701,925,626,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLines $l$ and $m$ are parallel and points $A$, $B$, and $D$ are collinear. What is the value of $x$?\n\n[asy]\n\nunitsize(1.1 inch);\n\ndraw((0,0)--(4,0),Arrows);\n\ndraw((0,1)--(4,1),Arrows);\n\ndraw((3,2)--(1,-1),Arrows);\n\ndot((0.3,0));\nlabel(\"$m$\",(0.3,0),N);\n\ndot((0.3,1));\nlabel(\"$l$\",(0.3,1),N);\n\ndot((3.7,0));\n\ndot((3.7,1));\nlabel(\"$C$\",(3.7,1),N);\n\ndot((1.2,-0.7));\n\ndot((2.8,1.7));\nlabel(\"$A$\",(2.8,1.7),NW);\n\ndot((2.34,1));\nlabel(\"$B$\",(2.34,1),NW);\nlabel(\"$5x-8^\\circ$\",(2.34,1),SW);\n\ndot((1.66,0));\nlabel(\"$D$\",(1.66,0),NW);\nlabel(\"$143^\\circ$\",(1.66,0),SE);\n\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"36619925e33b26feb03047c34b2654ae5ced5ca5905bdbf73ea159549130d92a"},"seconds":11.749017238616943,"seed":1052896390837156415,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for \\( x \\) given the geometric configuration, we need to analyze the angles formed by the parallel lines and the transversal.\n\n1. **Identify the given angles:**\n   - The angle at point \\( A \\) is labeled as \\( 5x - 8^\\circ \\).\n   - The angle at point \\( D \\) is labeled as \\( 143^\\circ \\).\n\n2. **Understand the relationship between the angles:**\n   - Since lines \\( l \\) and \\( m \\) are parallel, and \\( AD \\) is a transversal, the angle at point \\( D \\) (which is \\( 143^\\circ \\)) and the angle at point \\( B \\) (which is \\( 5x - 8^\\circ \\)) are corresponding angles or co-interior angles, depending on their positions relative to the transversal and the parallel lines.\n\n3. **Determine the type of angles:**\n   - Since the angle at point \\( D \\) is \\( 143^\\circ \\) and the angle at point \\( B \\) is \\( 5x - 8^\\circ \\), and these angles are supplementary (they add up to \\( 180^\\circ \\) because they form a straight line when extended), we can set up the equation:\n     \\[\n     5x - 8^\\circ + 143^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n     \\]\n\n4. **Solve the equation:**\n   \\[\n   5x - 8^\\circ + 143^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   5x + 135^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   5x = 180^\\circ - 135^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   5x = 45^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{45^\\circ}{5}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = 9^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{9}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{9}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:193"}
